// REJECTS: Unexpected token '<EOF>'. Valid alternatives: [',', ')']
//
// A `#{` graph fetch island closed with a plain ')' instead of `}#`. The parser runs to
// end-of-input rather than accepting the enclosing delimiter as a terminator.
//
// unterminated-embedded-data.pure pins the same failure mode for a ###Data island; this
// one matters separately because the graph fetch island lives INSIDE an expression, where
// a ')' is genuinely expected soon (it is the argument list of graphFetch). A rewrite that
// scans for a closing bracket to delimit the island -- rather than requiring the '}#'
// digraph -- has a plausible-looking candidate right there, truncates the tree at it, and
// produces a model that parses with properties missing.
###Pure
Class fixture::neg::Cat
{
   name: String[1];
}

function fixture::neg::unterminatedTree(): meta::pure::metamodel::type::Any[*]
{
   fixture::neg::Cat.all()->graphFetch(#{
      fixture::neg::Cat {
         name
      }
   )
}
